===========================================================================
SCOPE — WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER
===========================================================================

COVERED (the "Software"): everything under code/, supplementary/, docs/ and
external_validation/code/, plus the notebook and the build and verification
scripts. Reuse these freely under the MIT terms above.

NOT COVERED: patient-derived material. The PREDIX HER2 trial data and every
artefact derived from it remain under the trial's own governance and the
consent given by its participants. That includes any input matrix under data/,
and it includes results/, report/ and report figures and tables, because those
carry individual-level information: per-patient fold membership, treatment arm,
the pCR outcome, predicted probabilities, and within-fold standardised values
of most curated metrics. Read docs/NO_PATIENT_DATA.md, which quantifies exactly what individual-level
information remains once the input matrix is withheld.

Nothing in the MIT grant above conveys any right to redistribute, publish or
re-identify patient-derived material, and no such right is implied by that
material appearing in this repository. Requests should go to the study's data
controller.

THIRD-PARTY DATA: the external cohort files under data/ are derived metrics
computed from public GEO series (I-SPY2, GSE194040; NCT02326974, GSE243375).
They carry the terms of those original studies and should be attributed to
them, and so do the artefacts derived from them — the per-cohort tables
under external_validation/, which
hold a predicted probability and an outcome for each of those cohorts'
patients. They are patient-derived too, and the MIT grant does not reach them
either. The TransNEO metrics used in external_validation/ are NOT redistributed
here for that reason.

Licence text generated 2026-09-06.

===========================================================================
THIS IS THE NO-PATIENT-DATA VARIANT
===========================================================================

The PREDIX individual-level input matrix (`data/clin_multiomics_curated_metrics_PREDIX_HER2_new.txt`,
197 patients) is deliberately NOT deposited here, because
whether the trial's ethics approval and participant consent permit its public
release is a question for the study's data controller, not a build step.

Removing it removed the trial's `patientID` values. **It did not remove the
individual-level information.** The deposited cross-validation artefacts under
results/ still carry, per patient, the pCR outcome, thousands of predicted
probabilities, fold membership, treatment arm, and the within-fold standardised
values of most curated metrics. docs/NO_PATIENT_DATA.md quantifies exactly what
remains. Read it before treating this tree as anonymous — it is not.

The MIT grant above covers the software only and conveys no rights over any of
that material.
